From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:40:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 50/66] uclient: send a request without waiting for the delayed
 ACK

uclient-http writes a request as several small writes (request line,
each header, the body), and with Nagle every write after the first
waited for the server's delayed ACK, adding about 40 ms to a short
request (B80; Aeolus sets TCP_QUICKACK on its manager to work around
it). Add a patch that sets TCP_NODELAY on the connection, as curl does
by default.

Bump PKG_RELEASE.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 package/libs/uclient/Makefile                 |  2 +-
 ...-without-waiting-for-the-delayed-ACK.patch | 46 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 47 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 package/libs/uclient/patches/100-uclient-http-send-a-request-without-waiting-for-the-delayed-ACK.patch

diff --git a/package/libs/uclient/Makefile b/package/libs/uclient/Makefile
index 4012f07593..da1dcd29a1 100644
--- a/package/libs/uclient/Makefile
+++ b/package/libs/uclient/Makefile
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=uclient
-PKG_RELEASE=1
+PKG_RELEASE=2
 
 PKG_SOURCE_PROTO:=git
 PKG_SOURCE_URL=$(PROJECT_GIT)/project/uclient.git
diff --git a/package/libs/uclient/patches/100-uclient-http-send-a-request-without-waiting-for-the-delayed-ACK.patch b/package/libs/uclient/patches/100-uclient-http-send-a-request-without-waiting-for-the-delayed-ACK.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..c90eafa071
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/libs/uclient/patches/100-uclient-http-send-a-request-without-waiting-for-the-delayed-ACK.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+From d6010cc35780c2dec24d65b21e700db5e7d18273 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
+Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:40:03 -0500
+Subject: [PATCH] uclient-http: send a request without waiting for the delayed
+ ACK
+
+A request goes out in several small writes: the request line, each
+header, the end of the headers and then the body, each through its own
+ustream_printf(). With Nagle's algorithm on, every write after the first
+waits until the server acknowledges the previous one, and a server that
+has not answered yet delays that ACK by about 40 ms, so a short request
+takes 40 ms longer than it should. Set TCP_NODELAY on the connection,
+as curl does by default.
+
+Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
+Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
+---
+ uclient-http.c | 5 +++++
+ 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)
+
+diff --git a/uclient-http.c b/uclient-http.c
+index 04ddcb9..a93b513 100644
+--- a/uclient-http.c
++++ b/uclient-http.c
+@@ -16,6 +16,8 @@
+  * OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE USE OR PERFORMANCE OF THIS SOFTWARE.
+  */
+ #include <sys/socket.h>
++#include <netinet/in.h>
++#include <netinet/tcp.h>
+ #include <stdio.h>
+ #include <ctype.h>
+ #include <unistd.h>
+@@ -155,6 +157,9 @@ static int uclient_do_connect(struct uclient_http *uh, const char *port)
+ 		return -1;
+ 
+ 	fcntl(fd, F_SETFL, fcntl(fd, F_GETFL) | O_NONBLOCK);
++	/* a request goes out in several small writes; with Nagle each one
++	 * after the first would wait for the server's delayed ACK */
++	setsockopt(fd, IPPROTO_TCP, TCP_NODELAY, &(int){ 1 }, sizeof(int));
+ 	uh->fd = fd;
+ 
+ 	sl = sizeof(uh->uc.local_addr);
+-- 
+2.43.0
+
